# HappenMCR nginx — host hygiene (Contabo)

Paste into the server block(s) that handle `happenmcr.com` / `www.happenmcr.com`.
Goal: **one hop** from any http/www variant → `https://happenmcr.com$request_uri`.

Today Google still sees chains like:

`http://www.happenmcr.com/` → 301 `https://www.happenmcr.com/` → 308 `https://happenmcr.com/`

That shows up in Search Console as **Duplicate without user-selected canonical**.

## Recommended server blocks

```nginx
# Catch plain HTTP for both apex and www → HTTPS apex (one hop)
server {
    listen 80;
    listen [::]:80;
    server_name happenmcr.com www.happenmcr.com;
    return 301 https://happenmcr.com$request_uri;
}

# HTTPS www → HTTPS apex (one hop)
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name www.happenmcr.com;

    # ssl_certificate / ssl_certificate_key — same certs as apex (SAN must include www)

    return 301 https://happenmcr.com$request_uri;
}

# Canonical HTTPS apex
server {
    listen 443 ssl http2;
    listen [::]:443 ssl http2;
    server_name happenmcr.com;

    # ssl_certificate / ssl_certificate_key …

    # Existing proxy_pass to Next on :3000 and /api → :4000 stay here.
    location / {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:3000;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
        proxy_set_header Upgrade $http_upgrade;
        proxy_set_header Connection "upgrade";
    }

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://127.0.0.1:4000/;
        proxy_http_version 1.1;
        proxy_set_header Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Host $host;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-Proto $scheme;
        proxy_set_header X-Forwarded-For $proxy_add_x_forwarded_for;
    }
}
```

## Apply on Contabo

```bash
sudo nginx -t
sudo systemctl reload nginx

# Verify ONE hop each
curl -sI --max-redirs 0 http://www.happenmcr.com/ | grep -iE 'HTTP/|location:'
curl -sI --max-redirs 0 https://www.happenmcr.com/ | grep -iE 'HTTP/|location:'
curl -sI --max-redirs 0 http://happenmcr.com/ | grep -iE 'HTTP/|location:'
```

Expected: each returns `301` (or `308`) with `Location: https://happenmcr.com/` — never `https://www.…`.
